{"nodes": [{"chunk_id": "node1", "text": "Lecture Notes: Introduction to Distributed Systems", "structural_type": "heading", "semantic_category": "header"}, {"chunk_id": "node2", "text": "1. Replication and Consistency models guarantee state agreements.", "structural_type": "list_item", "semantic_category": "body_text"}, {"chunk_id": "node3", "text": "2. Vector clocks are used to capture causal relationships in messages.", "structural_type": "list_item", "semantic_category": "body_text"}, {"chunk_id": "node4", "text": "3. Raft uses leader election and consensus to replicate logs safely.", "structural_type": "list_item", "semantic_category": "body_text"}, {"chunk_id": "node5", "text": "4. Paxos is another consensus algorithm but is harder to implement", "structural_type": "list_item", "semantic_category": "body_text"}, {"chunk_id": "node6", "text": "5. Byzantine fault tolerance handles arbitrary failures including malicious actors.", "structural_type": "list_item", "semantic_category": "body_text"}]}